   "result_summary": "The 2001-07-21 consolidation is committed as `a32ea683`. Both gates (`lint.py` and `sleep-audit.py`) passed on the first try. I did not push, because the replay instructions say the runner pushes after its own checks.\n\nAll 31 messages with notes from week 2001-W29 were handled. Thirty went into existing topic files, each line linked to its source message. The main items:\n- the owner agreed to referee a swing-option paper for Risk Magazine, report due 14 Aug\n- he sent Duffie the \"Reliability Var\" paper as the first document for audit\n- Toshiba's Dr. Uenohara may visit Houston 31 Jul–4 Aug\n- Christian Werner wants to move from Sydney to Houston, but Paul Quilkey has not released him\n- the \"Changes at EBS\" memo\n- the owner's family is moving back to Houston from California\n\nThe one dropped message is m08738 (a calendar-delegate request), listed as logistics in `dataset/drops/sleep-090.tsv`. Glen Dixon reached five messages with notes, so he now has `memory/people/glen-dixon.md` and a line in the alias table. \"Debra\" stays unlinked because the bare name also matches a different Debra at Rice from 2000.\n\nMost files I touched were already over their size target. In 16 of them, the oldest lines moved word-for-word to `memory/archive/<domain>/2001/*-2001-07-21.md` so the files would not grow. No file was above 90% of its ceiling, so the rule to shrink three such files had nothing to act on.\n\nThe indexes, `state.md` and the run log are updated, and the processed inbox files are in `memory/archive/inbox/`. No question was due, and the inbox had no sleep-task or feedback blocks. The five oldest ongoing lines are still valid."
